{"kind":"request","text":"Model card histories around unknown outcomes and retained reads\n\nScope: section 5 of report 7f7def61 (attachments/testing-strategy.md). Three repairs came from card histories that one-at-a-time tests missed: 8ea69d43 (cards reopened on the process their calls reached), ee6e7d1f (a ten-second wait expired during an 11.6-second signed read) and ebc1e608 (a truncated retained result was treated as complete). The Goose follow-up 95cdd559 adds a fourth: the card's own 120-second wait (TOOL_WAIT_MS in packages/mcp/browser/bridge.ts) showed a timeout while the server's reply arrived later, and the card did not recover.\n\nGenerate open, read, press, timeout, late reply, process switch, refresh, supersede, explicit retry and teardown commands. Keep a separate test ledger, smaller than ViewSessions: the active view, the displayed cut, the pending original request, the signature count and whether a result is complete or truncated.\n\nProperties: uncertainty never repeats a write on its own; a stale or superseded request signs nothing before admission; a complete retained answer replays without signing; an explicit retry of a truncated read signs one new read; closing the bridge settles each pending request once; the receiving process opens a missing view before dispatch. Add the late-reply property: a reply that arrives after the card's wait expired settles the original request in the ledger, and the card offers a visible way to read it without a second write.\n\nDistinguishing histories: read, timeout, late return, check the original; retained truncated read, explicit retry, complete; open on process A, dispatch through process B. Use gates and fake timers, never elapsed sleeps. Budget about 100 short plain histories and four fixed browser histories.\n\nVerify with npx vitest run --project mcp view-sessions and the Card workflow at the exact head. If the late-reply property fails on current source, keep the failing history as a named case and propose the bridge correction in the same head or a separate child; do not change TOOL_WAIT_MS alone to pass.\n\nOrder: after e13960b4. The O4 live runs take precedence whenever the browser connection returns.","body":{"conditions":"Reviewed head lands on main with the history model, the named distinguishing histories and a Card workflow pass at the exact head.","target_head":"da94f450048723d2f40e22a0273b745ebb34bf75","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}